<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Halvad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Halvad is a town in Morbi district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhalawad">Jhalawad</a> region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-rann-of-kutch">Little Rann of Kutch</a>. Founded in the late 15th century as the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhala">Jhala Rajputs</a>, it remained their capital until the court moved to Dhrangadhra in the 18th century, and several Jhala states, including Wankaner, Wadhwan and Lakhtar, were founded by cadets of the Halvad house.</p></div>
